  "independently_expected_cases": [
    "For arbitrary ordered payload type, empty worker input has scan mean 0 and source mean 2 for every rank.",
    "Valid singleton has scan mean 1 and source mean 9; invalid rank 1 on [7] has scan mean 1 and source mean 11.",
    "For worker rank 0 on [0,1], the already checked actual index paths have W=2 or 3 and T=11 or 20, each with probability 1/2: E[W]=5/2 and E[T]=31/2.",
    "For rank 1 on [x,x], both indexed choices have W=2; source costs 12 and 13 have equal probabilities, giving E[W]=2 and E[T]=25/2.",
    "The pair scan recurrence has immediate toll 2 and only the pivot-1 singleton child: E[W_2]=2+(1/2)E[W_1].",
    "For any input and worker rank, bounded scalar supports give real integrability; the initial scan gives n<=E[W], the triangular pathwise bound gives E[W]<=n(n+1)/2, and the common-run bridge gives E[W]<=E[T]<=9E[W]+2."
  ],
  "stage_scope": "Add nonnegative weighted expectations of the existing run, derive their exact conditional one-child equation and the scan recurrence, connect the existing Nat scalar laws to standard lower/real integrals, prove finiteness/integrability and initial/quadratic/affine expectation bounds, and retain connected exact cases.",
